    <string name="first_run_page_one_label">Step 1 of 2</string>
    <string name="first_run_page_two_label">Step 2 of 2</string>
    <string name="first_run_statement_title">Terms of Use</string>
    <string name="first_run_statement_section">1. This app is completely free. If you paid for it, request a refund immediately and contact the author to verify and report the seller.</string>
    <string name="first_run_statement_body">2. This app is only used to replace, back up, and restore Unreal Engine configuration files for Wuthering Waves on Android devices. Except for actions you explicitly initiate, the app does not parse or upload your game configurations or other local files. Some features require an internet connection, such as announcements and update checks.\n\n3. This app is open source on GitHub, and some content was created with AI assistance. To reduce the risk of tampered packages, download it only from the author’s cloud drive or other official release channels. Packages from unknown sources may pose security risks and may harm your device or data.</string>
    <string name="first_run_section_notice_bracketed">[Safety notice]</string>
    <string name="first_run_notice_test_body">1. This app requires Shizuku or Root authorization to work properly. For security and ease of use, Shizuku is recommended. An activation tutorial is available on the author’s Bilibili page. If you still need help, join the QQ group from Settings.\n\n2. Replacing the game’s original engine configuration may increase device heat and power consumption and may affect frame-rate stability. Choose a graphics preset appropriate for your device. To restore the default graphics, restore the original game configuration from the Backup page.\n\n3. The current version may still contain unknown issues. Follow the in-app instructions carefully. If you encounter a problem, export and share a runtime log from Settings to help the developer diagnose and improve the app.</string>
    <string name="first_run_section_usage_bracketed">[Instructions]</string>
    <string name="first_run_usage_test_body">1. Before first use, authorize this app through Shizuku or a Root manager. Continue only after the home page shows that the permission service is ready.\n\n2. Make sure Wuthering Waves is installed and has been launched normally at least once so that the required configuration directory exists. Fully exit the game before replacing or restoring configurations.\n\n3. Open Configuration, select an installed game server, and choose the Low, Medium, High, or Extreme preset according to your device. Confirm the selection, tap “Replace graphics”, and wait for the operation to finish.\n\n4. To use game resolution correction, watch the tutorial on Bilibili. This process cannot be described accurately in text; thank you for understanding.\n\n5. To undo a graphics change, open Backup and restore either the original game configuration or an existing configuration backup. Confirm the selected server before restoring.</string>
